 10. 🏈 1 fun thing: College football reveal 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 College Football Playoff via X Miami, Georgia, Utah and Indiana nabbed the top 4 spots in the first College Football Playoff rankings released last night, Axios' Donica Phifer writes. 

 Why it matters: The final of six weekly rankings will determine the bracket for the 12-team playoff. UCLA — one of just three undefeated teams along with Miami and Utah — was ranked No. 8 because of a weak schedule.

 Ohio State (6-2) is the first team out of the playoffs. If the regular season ended today, No. 25 Boise State would make it in as the best team from a non-major conference. Go deeper . 

 
 
